# Security

Treat user input, model output, retrieved documents, websites, files, external APIs, MCP results, and tool output as untrusted. None of them may change system policy, grant tools, read secrets, or authorize destructive action.

Validate tool arguments in code before execution. Authorize the tenant and the resource on every privileged path.

Do not log secrets, session tokens, or raw credentials. Sensitive prompt and user content needs an explicit logging decision.

Security review is required for auth, authorization, secrets, uploads, external URLs, webhooks, filesystem access, agent tools, privileged actions, and arbitrary execution. A green test run does not replace that review.

Default privileges are the minimum the feature needs.
